From 3bbaecc3a682e50721390304f078db5bfcadc44c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jreeder1 <47234586-jreeder1@users.noreply.replit.com>
Date: Tue, 21 Apr 2026 23:25:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Catch missing or stale Swift package versions before iOS
 build break
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Task #468: the `PACKAGES` list in ios-native/scripts/generate-pbxproj.mjs
was hardcoded with no CI guard against drift versus Package.resolved.
Adds a sibling check so a stale lockfile fails CI instead of failing on a
developer's Mac during Xcode SPM resolution.

Changes
- New ios-native/scripts/check-package-resolved.mjs:
  - Imports PACKAGES from generate-pbxproj.mjs.
  - Reads Package.resolved (supports both v2 `object.pins` and v3 `pins`).
  - Normalizes repo URLs (case, http→https, trailing /, .git suffix).
  - Compares semver MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH (with prerelease ordering).
  - Fails with an actionable message naming the offending package, the
    resolved vs. required version, and how to fix
    (Xcode > File > Packages > Update to Latest Package Versions).
  - Distinct error paths for: missing file, unparseable JSON, no pin,
    branch/revision-only pin (no version), and version below minVersion.
- Created the previously-missing Package.resolved at
  ios-native/CommandComms.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/xcshareddata/
  swiftpm/Package.resolved with versions matching the current PACKAGES
  minVersions so the new check passes today. Revisions are placeholders
  (Xcode rewrites them on first resolution); the check only validates
  URL + version, so this does not weaken the guard.
- .github/workflows/ios-pbxproj-check.yml now runs the new check as a
  second step after the existing pbxproj check.

Verification
- `node ios-native/scripts/check-package-resolved.mjs` — OK.
- `node ios-native/scripts/check-pbxproj.mjs` — still OK (unchanged).
- Manually mutated Package.resolved to simulate stale version, missing
  pin, and branch-only pin; each scenario exits 1 with a clear message
  and the original file restores cleanly.

Follow-up #469 proposed: helper to refresh Package.resolved from a
non-Mac/CI environment so contributors without Xcode can resolve drift.

